        ],
        "geology": "The bedrock is composed of Neogene age sedimentary rock, classified in the Awa Group. In more detail, it is classified in Kiyosumi formation. Kiyosumi formation is flysch-type alternating sandstone and mudstone, and is characterized by a predominance of thicker turbidite sandstones.",
        "hydrology": "It rarely snows and most precipitation is rainfall. About 20% of rainfall deeply percolated and discharged without going through weirs [Oda et al., 2008]. The mean transit time was estimated as 1068 days [Oda et al., 2009].",
        "soils": "Soil is classified as Cambisol (brown forest soil). The average soil depth is 2.87 m in watershed A and 2.22 m in watershed B (Shiraki et al., 1999).",
        "vegetation": "Japanese cedar (Cryptomeria japonica) and some cypress (Chamaecyparis obtusa). "
